WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
The Forum in Rome.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.490
A raised platform, and
a packed crowd below it.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.330
Brutus speaks first: "Not
that I loved Caesar less,

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.660
but that I loved Rome more."

5
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.690
The crowd roars for him.

6
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.830
He leaves.

7
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.900
A second man climbs up
beside a covered bier:

8
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:23.290
"Friends, Romans, countrymen,
lend me your ears;" Same crowd.

9
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.530
Same day.

10
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.970
Minutes later, they want
to burn Brutus's house.

11
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.650
What did Antony do?

12
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.630
In this mission, you'll hear the
difference between prose and blank verse,

13
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.360
and who speaks in which.

14
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.950
You'll take apart Brutus's
speech, sentence by sentence.

15
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.600
And you'll listen for the words
Antony keeps coming back to.

16
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.300
Your mission: work out how
Antony turns the crowd.
